{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_839fecb69ec3fa12\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_839fecb69ec3fa12/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Unfindable or non-existent references\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_b269035d5f6ff3270d451b66\", \"member_8d50dd1c5f78296f69cc5bde\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports being unable to find the papers cited by both answers and asks whether anyone else is seeing this.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports finding references with journal names that do not exist on RP-7811 and asks whether to log this separately.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor replying in the thread about papers that cannot be found asks whether the reference is unfindable or points to a real but different source.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor replying about RP-7811 asks whether the reference is unfindable or points to a real but different source, and asks for the reference string to be preserved before the task disappears from the queue.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the thread about papers that cannot be found, the team lead instructs the thread starter to keep the source string and a lookup result with the flag so QA can distinguish fabricated references from broken links.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the RP-7811 thread, the team lead instructs the thread starter to keep the source string and a lookup result with the flag, distinguishing fabricated references from broken links and a mismatched DOI from an unreachable journal website.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current content-quality rubric treats fabricated references or materially unsupported attributions as major citation-support defects, and limited citation-detail errors with identifiable source and support as minor defects. An inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the claim's error grade. Task-quality defect grades do not determine operational incident severity.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"Neither supplied thread includes the source string and lookup result requested by the team lead, so these messages do not confirm whether the reported references are fabricated, mismatched or inaccessible.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The team lead's reply in the RP-7811 thread gives an evidence-preservation instruction but does not explicitly answer the QA tutor's separate-logging question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says to record that a dead-link citation could not be verified. A failed URL alone does not prove the factual claim false; access failure must be distinguished from unsupported attribution or a fabricated reference.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions distinguish a broken link, which is an access or verification failure, from an existing source that does not support the claim and from an invented reference.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors raise reference-verification concerns: one cannot find papers cited by both answers, and one reports non-existent journal names on RP-7811.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The team lead has asked for source strings and lookup results in both threads; the supplied messages do not include those inputs.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor in each thread asks whether the reference is unfindable or points to a real but different source; the QA tutor replying about RP-7811 also asks for the reference string to be preserved.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The QA tutor reporting RP-7811 asks whether to log the issue separately, but the team lead's reply does not explicitly settle separate logging.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says to record that a dead-link citation could not be verified and distinguish access failure from unsupported attribution or a fabricated reference.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current content-quality rubric treats fabricated references as major citation-support defects, but lack of access alone does not establish the factual claim's error grade.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:no_action\", \"kind\": \"NO_ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why no further action is needed now: The team lead has already supplied the immediate next step in both threads, and the requested lookup evidence is not shown. Current guidance supports distinguishing verification failure from fabricated or unsupported references rather than classifying these reports prematurely.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b269035d5f6ff3270d451b66\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b269035d5f6ff3270d451b66 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The QA tutor receives an evidence-preservation instruction from the team lead, but the supplied thread does not establish whether the cited papers exist or why they cannot be found.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_8d50dd1c5f78296f69cc5bde\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_8d50dd1c5f78296f69cc5bde is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead gives the QA tutor an immediate evidence-preservation step, but the supplied thread neither verifies the reported journal problem nor explicitly settles separate logging.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: Two QA tutors report reference concerns, but the supplied threads show a contained verification step already given by the team lead, not blocked work or conflicting scoring instructions. The reports do not establish broader disruption or systemic labeling risk.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U002\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U002 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U014\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U014 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911139.000011\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b269035d5f6ff3270d451b66\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911139.000011\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:18:59.000011Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Both answers cite papers I cannot find.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911194.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b269035d5f6ff3270d451b66\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911139.000011\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:19:54.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the reference unfindable, or does it point to a real but different source?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790911240.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b269035d5f6ff3270d451b66\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911139.000011\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:20:40.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Keep the source string and a lookup result with the flag; QA still needs to distinguish fabricated references from broken links.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927811.000013\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_8d50dd1c5f78296f69cc5bde\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927811.000013\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:56:51.000013Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U014\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? I'm finding references with journal names that don't exist. Do we log this separately? (task ref RP-7811)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927863.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_8d50dd1c5f78296f69cc5bde\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927811.000013\", \"author_id\": \"U019\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:57:43.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U014\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the reference unfindable, or does it point to a real but different source? Could you preserve the reference string before the task disappears from the queue?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790927913.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_8d50dd1c5f78296f69cc5bde\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927811.000013\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:58:33.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U014\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Keep the source string and a lookup result with the flag; QA still needs to distinguish fabricated references from broken links. A mismatched DOI is not the same problem as an unreachable journal website.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-submit-zoom-generalization-rejected@1.0:044e436d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-submit-zoom-generalization-rejected@1.0\", \"title\": \"Reject a universal browser-zoom remedy for Submit reports\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-submit-zoom-generalization-rejected\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-08T16:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-08T16:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"resolved_in_checked_tasks\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_rejected; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: resolved_in_checked_tasks) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nThe September 7 support notes cover RP14-Z011 and RP14-Z012 on a training workstation. At 200% browser zoom, the bottom of the form, including Submit, lay below the visible area. The button was not observed to be disabled. Returning the browser to 100% exposed the button, and both tasks produced a submission receipt: SIM-SUB-RP14-Z011 and SIM-SUB-RP14-Z012.\\n\\nNo network error or server rejection was recorded. These two cases were already resolved before this advice review; no action in response to the rejected recommendation has been executed.\\n\\n## Prior ThreadSense advice\\n\\nAdd a standard FAQ answer telling every tutor with a Submit problem to reset browser zoom to 100% before reporting the issue.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Calibration\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Calibration\\nFor comparable pairs receiving different judgments, retain both rationales and the relevant evidence. A scoped answer about one pair does not automatically become a new universal preference rule.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-submit-engineering-handoff@1.0:d84c905d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-submit-engineering-handoff@1.0\", \"title\": \"Submission incident handed to engineering; diagnosis remains open\", \"sections\": [\"Incident scope\", \"Advice and approval\", \"Handoff receipt\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-submit-engineering-handoff\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"escalation_receipt\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-28T17:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-28T17:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"handoff_recorded\", \"outcome_status\": \"open\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (escalation_receipt; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: handoff_recorded; outcome_status: open) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Incident scope\\nEarlier batch-15 reports RP15-S201, RP15-S202 and RP15-S203 described a disabled Submit button after the required fields were filled. The local record identifier is SIM-ENG-RP-20260928-01; it is a synthetic internal receipt, not a link to a real ticketing service.\\n\\n## Advice and approval\\nThe simulated Advisor recommended collecting field state, task IDs, time and button behavior, then escalating the report. Alex approved an engineering handoff.\\n\\n## Handoff receipt\\nAt 16:30 UTC on September 28, Alex recorded sending the three task references and screenshots to Daniel (U005, ENGINEER). Daniel's recorded acknowledgment at 16:45 UTC was: “Received these three examples. I can reproduce a disabled control in one trace; checking the validation state. No shared cause or repair is confirmed.”\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"Approve a JSON format for weekly audit manifests\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nThe September 24 QA handoff contained two audit manifests, RP15-AUD-01 and RP15-AUD-02, with filenames that omitted the batch. One used a prose list of task IDs; the other used a JSON array. Alex needed to combine the audit packets, not compare model answers.\\n\\nThe proposed administrative convention is a JSON object containing batch_id, audit_date, and task_ids, saved as rp15_audit_YYYY-MM-DD.json. Existing task ratings and rationales remain unchanged.\\n\\nThe review approves the convention and a short channel draft. At this cutoff the draft is not posted and no converted export has been checked.\\n\\n## Prior ThreadSense advice\\n\\nPublish one naming and JSON structure convention for QA weekly audit manifests so the handoff files can be combined without manual interpretation.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual secondary requirement | A stylistic choice that violates no requirement |\\n| Citation support | Fabricated reference or materially unsupported attribution | A limited citation-detail error where the source and support remain identifiable | A valid source that supports the claim |\\n| Preference | Identify a meaningful benefit; grade underlying defects separately | Do not manufacture a defect to break a tie | No meaningful quality difference supports a tie |\\n\\nAn inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the error grade of the claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Ties and preferences\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ADDED FOR TYPE COVERAGE: best-ranked faq for this query (rank 6), outside the top 5.]\\n## Ties and preferences\\n\\n### Q: How much improvement is needed to avoid a tie?\\nThe difference must offer a meaningful benefit to the user. Cosmetic phrasing alone usually does not. Explain that benefit; otherwise a tie can be appropriate.\\n\\n### Q: QA is reversing ties on similar pairs. What should I do?\\nShare the pairs, relevant prompt constraints and both rationales for calibration. Check whether the cases are actually comparable. An answer to one pair should not be generalized without matching its scope.\", \"retrieved_as\": {\"role\": \"TYPE_COVERAGE\", \"detail\": \"best-ranked faq for this query (rank 6), outside the top 5\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors\\n\\n### Q: What counts as a significant factual error?\\nAn error that changes the central conclusion or the answer the user would act on. A nonessential background detail with no effect on the recommendation is minor.\\n\\n### Q: The source link is dead. Should I penalize the factual claim?\\nRecord that the citation could not be verified. A failed URL alone does not prove the claim is false. Distinguish access failure from an unsupported attribution or fabricated reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors and citations\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors and citations\\n- A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\\n- A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n- A broken link is an access/verification failure, not proof that the underlying factual claim is false.\\n- Distinguish an existing source that does not support the claim from an invented reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration announcement\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789567200.700002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789567200.700002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00.700002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-16T14:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_14): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nPreference batch 14 calibration: choose a tie when neither answer offers a meaningful quality advantage. If choosing A or B, identify the user-facing benefit rather than saying only that it sounds nicer. Keep material factual or instruction-following defects separate. Bring both rationales for disputed pairs to the eight-pair calibration review. This message clarifies the existing criterion; it does not create a new numerical threshold.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:4745e3e0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Project purpose\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Project purpose\\nCompare two responses against the user's prompt. Record meaningful differences in factual accuracy, instruction adherence, citation support and usefulness.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0\", \"title\": \"TL rejects a universal JSON-first preference rule\", \"sections\": [\"Suggested advice\", \"TL response\", \"Consequence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-format-rule-rejected\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-23T16:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-23T16:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"REC